<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-23T13:00:34+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:00:34 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Started beach cleanup group at the age of 10, teen now wins 2026 Barron Prize]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134409922.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At 10, Caymus “CO” Maxson saw beach trash being raked towards the sea and decided to act. Six years later, her youth-led nonprofit Trash Turtles has removed over six tons of debris, cleaned 300+ miles of beaches and recycled 75,000 cigarette butts. Now based in California, Maxson has been named a 2026 Gloria Barron Prize winner.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-caymus-maxson-the-16-year-old-california-teen-who-started-trash-turtles-at-10-led-50-beach-cleanups-removed-6-tons-of-debris-recycled-75000-cigarette-butts-and-became-a-2026-barron-prize-winner/articleshow/134409922.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-caymus-maxson-the-16-year-old-california-teen-who-started-trash-turtles-at-10-led-50-beach-cleanups-removed-6-tons-of-debris-recycled-75000-cigarette-butts-and-became-a-2026-barron-prize-winner/articleshow/134409922.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T12:07:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134411509,imgsize-98019.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Tasmania removed invasive rice grass; fish species more than doubled in 3 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134408795.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tasmania’s Duck Bay wetland is showing signs of recovery after years of work to remove invasive rice grass. Circular Head Landcare has reduced the weed from about 50 hectares to five, allowing native saltmarsh plants to return. University of Tasmania scientists found fish species increased from five to 11, with yellow-eye mullet and other species returning to restored areas.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2020-tasmania-treated-invasive-rice-grass-in-duck-bay-three-years-later-fish-species-had-more-than-doubled-from-5-to-11-and-average-catches-rose-from-about-2-to-45-per-net/articleshow/134408795.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/in-2020-tasmania-treated-invasive-rice-grass-in-duck-bay-three-years-later-fish-species-had-more-than-doubled-from-5-to-11-and-average-catches-rose-from-about-2-to-45-per-net/articleshow/134408795.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T12:06:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134409858,imgsize-98650.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[97-year-old Brisbane bowls club saved in $6M deal after $1M higher offer rejected]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134427400.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-97-year-old-brisbane-bowls-club-facing-demolition-is-saved-in-a-6-million-deal-after-bowls-queensland-rejected-an-offer-1-million-higher-to-keep-both-greens/articleshow/134427400.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-97-year-old-brisbane-bowls-club-facing-demolition-is-saved-in-a-6-million-deal-after-bowls-queensland-rejected-an-offer-1-million-higher-to-keep-both-greens/articleshow/134427400.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T12:05:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134427473,imgsize-900168.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[England’s white-tailed eagles return after 240 years, with 9 wild-born chicks now]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134411623.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/england-released-its-first-6-white-tailed-eagles-in-2019-after-a-240-year-absence-by-2026-the-project-had-produced-9-wild-born-chicks-including-3-this-summer/articleshow/134411623.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/england-released-its-first-6-white-tailed-eagles-in-2019-after-a-240-year-absence-by-2026-the-project-had-produced-9-wild-born-chicks-including-3-this-summer/articleshow/134411623.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-22T22:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134411636,imgsize-917663.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Hampshire man returns magazine 132 years late, avoids $12,055 fine]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134427096.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-hampshire-man-returns-a-magazine-132-years-late-after-library-introduces-fine-freeze-avoiding-a-potential-12055-fine/articleshow/134427096.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-hampshire-man-returns-a-magazine-132-years-late-after-library-introduces-fine-freeze-avoiding-a-potential-12055-fine/articleshow/134427096.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T11:39:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134427380,imgsize-812847.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['White House access privilege, not right': DOJ cites national security behind Trump barring reporters]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134426616.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Trump administration has claimed the authority to restrict access for journalists to the White House. It argues that access is a privilege and not a right, citing national security concerns. The Justice Department emphasizes that First Amendment rights do not guarantee access to the complex. In response, CNN, MS NOW, and Politico are challenging these restrictions in federal court.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/white-house-access-privilege-not-right-doj-cites-national-security-behind-trump-barring-reporters/articleshow/134426616.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/white-house-access-privilege-not-right-doj-cites-national-security-behind-trump-barring-reporters/articleshow/134426616.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T11:05:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134426703,imgsize-40606.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Andrew Jackson's 1,200-acre estate to bury new 70,000-sq-ft visitor center to protect views]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134416912.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Plans are underway for a $132 million redevelopment of The Hermitage, focusing on its historic landscape. The new visitor and education center will be significantly underground to maintain sightlines and preserve history. State lawmakers approved $6 million in initial funding for the project, signaling public support. The Andrew Jackson Foundation aims to present a comprehensive history, including the stories of enslaved people.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tennessees-andrew-jackson-estate-spans-1200-acres-its-new-plan-puts-much-of-a-70000-square-foot-visitor-center-underground-so-the-building-does-not-interrupt-views-across-the-historic-landscape/articleshow/134416912.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/tennessees-andrew-jackson-estate-spans-1200-acres-its-new-plan-puts-much-of-a-70000-square-foot-visitor-center-underground-so-the-building-does-not-interrupt-views-across-the-historic-landscape/articleshow/134416912.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T09:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134419085